.TH VIEWME 1 "September 2026" "viewme 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viewme \- view a Markdown file in a clean popup window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viewme
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I FILE.md
.br
.B viewme
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B viewme
renders a Markdown file and shows it in its own small window, with no tabs or address bar.
It needs no third-party packages: Markdown is rendered by a built-in renderer, served from a tiny web server on the loopback interface, and displayed in a Chromium-style
.I app
window (Google Chrome, Chromium, Brave, Edge or Vivaldi).
If none of those is installed, the page opens in the default browser instead.
.PP
The command returns immediately and the window stays open on its own.
When the window is closed the server exits.
The page reloads by itself whenever the file changes on disk.
.PP
Use
.B \-
as the file name to read Markdown from standard input:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git log \-\-stat | viewme \-
.fi
.RE
.SH FEATURES
Headings with an outline sidebar and scroll tracking, tables with alignment, task lists, nested lists, blockquotes, GitHub-style alerts (\fB> [!NOTE]\fR), fenced code with light syntax highlighting and a copy button, images (including relative paths), links to other Markdown files, reference links, and a small safe subset of inline HTML (\fB<details>\fR, \fB<kbd>\fR, \fB<img>\fR and similar).
Scripts, event handlers and \fBjavascript:\fR URLs are removed.
.PP
Relative images and links are served from the project root, which is the nearest parent folder containing
.BR .git ,
or else the folder of the file.
Files outside that root are never served.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " light | dark | auto
Set the color theme. The choice is remembered.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WxH"
Window size in pixels. Default 1000x820.
.TP
.B \-\-fg
Stay in the foreground until the window is closed.
.TP
.B \-\-serve
Do not open a window. Serve the page and print its URL, for use with your own browser.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
In the window:
.TP
.B t
Toggle light and dark theme.
.TP
.B o
Show or hide the outline.
.TP
.B s
Show the raw Markdown source.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIEWME_BROWSER
Path or name of the browser to use instead of auto-detection. It must accept Chromium's
.B \-\-app=URL
flag to get the popup style.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The theme is stored in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/viewme/config.json ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/viewme/config.json .
.SH SECURITY
The server listens on 127.0.0.1 only, on a random port.
Every request needs a random per-run token that is handed to the window in a cookie, the Host header is checked, and the page carries a strict Content Security Policy.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the file is missing or no display is available, 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
viewme README.md
viewme \-\-theme dark notes/todo.md
viewme \-\-serve docs/guide.md
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cpop (1)
